n an inquiry as to the stamp duty with which the instrument to which it relates is chargeable; and\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 unless such declaration is shown not to be true in any material respect, the person by whom it is made shall, on payment of the stamp duty chargeable upon the instrument, be relieved from any punishment to which he may be liable under }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 section 11}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 .\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (6)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Every instrument stamped under this section with a stamp or by way of a stamp certificate denoting that it is not chargeable with stamp duty or that it is duly stamped shall be admissible in evidence and available for all purposes notwithstanding any objection relating to stamp duty.}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Amended }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 21 of 2003 s. 5}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (7)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Where in respect of any instrument which is not stamped the Collector is required by any person under this section before or within the time for stamping such instrument to express his opinion under subsection (1) and such instrument is in the opinion of the Collector chargeable with stamp duty, the instrument\u8212??\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 may be stamped upon payment of the stamp duty if the stamp duty is paid not later than the time for stamping such instrument or the expiration of a period of 1 month from the date on which the assessment of the stamp duty is made, whichever is the later; or\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 if the stamp duty is not so paid, may be so stamped thereafter upon payment of the stamp duty and a penalty calculated under }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 section 9}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0  and, for that purpose, }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 section 9}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0  shall apply in relation to the stamping of such instrument as it applies in relation to the stamping of an instrument chargeable with stamp duty which is not stamped before or within the time for stamping such instrument.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (8)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Where notice of an assessment of the stamp duty chargeable on any instrument is, within 7 days from the date on which the assessment is made, served by post on any person who required the Collector to express his opinion with reference thereto under subsection (1) or who is liable for stamping such instrument, such assessment shall, after the expiration of a period of 1 month from that date, be final and conclusive for all purposes as against such person except if and to the extent that an appeal made against it under }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 section 14}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  succeeds.}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Amended }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 36 of 1994 s. 2}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (9)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 If, within a period of 1 month from the date on which an assessment is made of the stamp duty chargeable on any instrument, it appears to the Collector that the amount of the stamp duty so assessed is excessive, he may cancel such assessment and make such other assessment in substitution therefor as he may deem proper; and any reference in this Ordinance to an assessment shall be construed as including a reference to an assessment as so substituted. \par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (10)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Where the payment of stamp duty is denoted on any instrument chargeable with stamp duty or on any stamp certificate issued for the instrument, in respect of which the Collector expresses or is required to express his opinion under subsection (1) and the amount of the payment so denoted is less than the amount assessed by the Collector, then, without prejudice to the liability of any person for the payment of the difference between the amount of the stamp duty so denoted and the assessment, the instrument shall be chargeable, unless it is stamped in respect of the difference not later than 1 month from the date on which the assessment is made, with additional stamp duty of an amount equal to interest on the amount of the difference at the rate of 4 cents per $100 or part thereof per day in respect of the period beginning on the expiration of a period of 1 month from that date and ending on the date of the payment of such additional stamp duty; and the person or persons liable for stamping such instrument in respect of the stamp duty so assessed shall be the person or persons liable for stamping it in respect of such additional stamp duty.}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Amended }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 21 of 2003 s. 5}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (11)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 The Collector may remit, wholly or in part, any additional stamp duty payable under subsection (10).\par }}
